## 2. Codebase Structure & Key Components

The project structure is neat, modular, and separates concerns effectively:

```
gymweb1/
├── public/
│   └── assets/
│       ├── images/      # High-quality gym backgrounds and discipline images
│       └── videos/      # Grayscale video loops for the hero section
├── src/
│   ├── components/      # UI components (Header, Hero, Classes, Membership, etc.)
│   ├── hooks/           # Reusable custom React hooks
│   ├── App.jsx          # Entry page routing/assembly
│   ├── index.css        # Tailwind directives and custom brutalist scrollbars
│   └── main.jsx         # React DOM mounting
├── tailwind.config.js   # Custom theme, keyframes, fonts, and colors
└── vite.config.js       # Vite build configurations
```

### Key Engineering Highlights
1. **`CustomCursor.jsx` (Dynamic Theme & Hover Text)**
   - Traverses the DOM under the cursor in real-time to compute the active background color.
   - Dynamically adapts its styling depending on whether it's hovering over dark `#0D0D0D`, red `#B3000C`, or light background elements.
   - Enhances interactive elements by expanding and displaying status text (e.g. `VIEW`, `JOIN`, `CLICK`).
2. **`KineticTypography.jsx` (Accessible Text Entrance)**
   - Animates headings character-by-character on scroll using custom Cubic-Bezier timing arrays.
   - Safely addresses accessibility: embeds `aria-hidden="true"` on animated nodes and provides an `sr-only` tag containing the full text for screen readers.
   - Respects user operating system configurations via `useReducedMotion()`.
3. **`useMagnetic.js` (Magnetic Pull Interactions)**
   - Draws call-to-action buttons slightly toward the cursor when hovering, giving the application a highly premium, tactile feel.

